---
title: "Loading Rows"
description: "Display skeleton rows while Client-Side Row Model data is loading."
---

The Client-Side Row Model can display skeleton rows instead of the loading overlay while row data is loading.

## Enabling Loading Rows

Set `loading` to `LoadingOptions` with `type='rows'` to display loading rows.
Ten rows are displayed by default, or set `rowCount` to configure the number displayed.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    loading: {
        type: 'rows',
        rowCount: 10,
    },
};
```

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["loading"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Loading Rows" name="client-side-loading-rows" /%}

Loading rows are visual placeholders and are not included in Client-Side Row Model operations such as sorting, filtering, grouping or selection.
When loading finishes, set `loading=false` to display the row data.

## Custom Loading Cells

Loading rows use the [Loading Cell Component](./component-loading-cell-renderer/). Set `loadingCellRenderer` and `loadingCellRendererParams` on a column definition to customise that column, or set them as grid options to customise every loading cell.

The following example uses a custom loading component for the Athlete column while the other columns retain the default skeleton effect.

